# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# .env is gitignored and will never be committed.

# API key to the aiapi gateway project. Needed for anything that calls a model
# — compiling, healing, AI-executed steps, errands — while a fully compiled
# test replays without one (stories/keyless-replay-and-gateway-env.md).
# Left blank here on purpose: a blank line blocks the machine-wide key too.
AI_API_KEY=

# Which model the aiapi gateway should route to.
# Optional — leave blank to use the project default in src/config/defaults.ts.
AI_MODEL=
#openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash:nitro
#openrouter/google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview:nitro
#openrouter/google/gemini-3-flash-preview:nitro (favourite, fast, cheap)
#openrouter/google/gemma-4-31b-it:nitro (cheap, fast)
#openrouter/google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:nitro (not so smart)
#openrouter/google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free (mostly doesn't work)

# The OpenAI-compatible endpoint that gateway-routed models (gateway/… and
# aibroker/…) go through: a hosted broker, your org's internal gateway, a local
# bridge. There is no built-in one, so a gateway-routed model REFUSES to run
# until this is set — here, or once for every project in the machine .env.
# Commented out because the default model (openai/…) goes straight to OpenAI and
# needs only AI_API_KEY. Beats `ai.gatewayUrl` in steptix.config.json, same as
# AI_MODEL beats `ai.model`, so nothing tracked has to change to point one
# project elsewhere.
#AI_GATEWAY_URL=https://llm.corp.example
#AI_MODEL=gateway/openai/chatgpt-5.5

# Claude in your OWN AWS account, via Amazon Bedrock (stories/bedrock-provider.md).
# For a team whose approved AI is "Bedrock in our account": your region, your
# AWS agreement, your network path — commonly a VPC endpoint, so nothing goes
# over the public internet. Works headless and in CI.
#
# FIRST: npm install @anthropic-ai/bedrock-sdk
# It is an optional peer of @pkent/aigateway, not a dependency of this project —
# it pulls ~50 AWS packages, and only Bedrock users should pay for them. Forget
# it and the first AI call fails with missing_optional_dependency naming that
# command.
#
# The AWS_* half does NOT belong in this file. AWS_REGION, AWS_PROFILE and any
# AWS credentials are read straight from process.env by the AWS SDK, which knows
# nothing about these env files — so they belong in the environment that STARTS
# the server (or that runs your CI job), exactly like the proxy variables below.
# That is also how AWS credentials work everywhere else: from the machine, an
# SSO login or an instance role, never from a file in the repo.
#
# Putting them here does work for `steptix run` and the Electron Runner UI, which
# load this file into their own process at startup. It silently does NOT work
# on the Steptix / MCP path: the Sessions API server serves many projects and
# deliberately exports none of their .env files into its own process
# (stories/project-scoped-data-dir-and-env.md), and it forwards only AI_API_KEY,
# AI_MODEL and AI_GATEWAY_URL from a project's .env into the run. Set the AWS
# variables on the machine and all four paths agree.
#
# AWS_REGION is REQUIRED and there is no fallback worth relying on: unlike the
# Python SDK, the TypeScript client does not read ~/.aws/config, so an SSO
# profile that already carries a region is not enough.
#
# Model ids normally carry a cross-region inference prefix (global./eu./us.).
# That is the norm, not an edge case: AWS serves most current Claude models
# through inference profiles only, and the bare base id returns HTTP 400 asking
# for a profile id. The suffix varies per model (-v1, -20250929-v1:0, or none).
#
# Two ways to authenticate. Bearer token, which is an ordinary key:
#AI_MODEL=bedrock/global.anthropic.claude-opus-4-6-v1
#AI_API_KEY=<bedrock bearer token>
#   …and in the machine environment: AWS_REGION=eu-west-1
#
# …or nothing at all, and let the AWS credential chain sign each request —
# env credentials, an SSO profile, or an instance role. This is the mode with
# NO AI_API_KEY: leave the AI_API_KEY= line at the top of this file blank rather
# than deleting it — an absent key is filled from the machine-wide one at
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\steptix\.env, and AWS takes any key it is handed as a bearer
# token, which switches SigV4 off. Note the framework then reports AI as
# configured anyway, because the provider supplies its own credentials. To force
# a no-AI run there, use `ai.allowInRuns: false` in steptix.config.json — with no
# key to blank, that is the switch.
#AI_MODEL=bedrock/eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0
#   …and in the machine environment: AWS_REGION=eu-west-1, AWS_PROFILE=acme-dev

# Corporate proxy / TLS interception is NOT configured here. NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY,
# HTTPS_PROXY and NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS are read by the Node runtime at startup,
# before any framework code runs, so they belong in the environment that STARTS
# the server. NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS is filtered out of a project's .env on purpose
# (UNSAFE_CHILD_ENV_KEYS in src/mcp/server-start.ts): one Sessions API server
# serves every project pointing at that SERVER_URL, so a CA trusted for one
# would be trusted for all. See "Corporate networks" in README.md.

# How hard the model thinks on ROUTINE steps (the per-step action loop).
# Optional - leave blank for today's behaviour: nothing is sent and nothing
# changes. Values: low, medium, high, xhigh, max (also none/minimal).
#
# DO NOT use "none" - it is not the cheap option. Unset is. Measured on
# Anthropic Opus 4.8: unset averaged 91 output tokens, low 139, none 150.
# Turning thinking off does not stop the model reasoning, it moves the
# reasoning into the VISIBLE reply - which the runner parses as a JSON action
# list, so the commentary lands inside the JSON and the step fails to parse.
# responseFormat json_object does not protect you; Anthropic ignores it.
# Setting it also raises the routine output cap to 8192, because reasoning
# tokens count against the same cap as the answer - raising effort without
# raising the cap truncates the reply.
# Authoring calls (code-behind, assertions, failure diagnosis) already run at
# high effort and are NOT lowered by this.
AI_EFFORT=

# STEPTIX_SERVER_API_KEY is deliberately NOT listed here (stories/machine-key.md):
# it lives machine-wide at %LOCALAPPDATA%\steptix\.env (~/.steptix/.env elsewhere)
# and `steptix serve` generates it there on first start. Set it in a project .env
# only to pin a different key for a dedicated server.

# Open the last generated HTML report in the OS default browser after `run` completes.
# Skipped automatically when CI is set. Values: true/false/1/0/yes/no.
OPEN_REPORT_IN_BROWSER_AFTER_RUN=false

# After each test completes, append a "Latest runs" section at the bottom of the
# test .md file linking to its generated HTML reports (keeps the last 10).
# Values: true/false/1/0/yes/no.
APPEND_RUN_HISTORY_TO_TEST_FILE=false
